breach.segment:
// PostgreSQL engine marker: excludes MySQL / SQL Server replicas that share this metric.
// Keep instances that reported num_backends, or that reported no network/connections
// (MySQL / SQL Server only) in the window, so a replica that does not report every
// PostgreSQL engine metric is still covered.
WHERE (pg > 0 OR COALESCE(conn, 0) == 0) AND lag_n > 0
// Require ~5 minutes of lag samples so one late sample cannot trigger
| WHERE lag_n >= 5
// Alert threshold (seconds): the replica stayed behind its primary for the WHOLE
// window (the minimum lag is above the threshold), i.e. it is not catching up
// after bursts. Lower for latency-sensitive read traffic; raise for cross-region
// replicas or batch-heavy primaries.
| WHERE lag_min >= 120
| KEEP database_id, lag_min, lag_max, network_lag_max
| SORT lag_min DESC
| LIMIT 100
